WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:04.652 --> 00:00:09.791 line:88% position:50% align:center
Lesson six: system administration,
oversight and best practices.

2
00:00:10.852 --> 00:00:14.983 line:88% position:50% align:center
In this final lesson, we'll look at
the administrator's responsibilities,

3
00:00:14.993 --> 00:00:19.299 line:88% position:50% align:center
how the platform is built, and the
habits that keep its records reliable.

4
00:00:21.219 --> 00:00:24.191 line:88% position:50% align:center
Administrators carry a
special responsibility,

5
00:00:24.201 --> 00:00:28.403 line:88% position:50% align:center
because they control the platform's
structure and its financial decisions.

6
00:00:29.452 --> 00:00:33.531 line:88% position:50% align:center
They set up projects accurately,
with correct references and budgets,

7
00:00:33.541 --> 00:00:36.356 line:88% position:50% align:center
and they manage team
leaders, their credentials,

8
00:00:36.366 --> 00:00:38.315 line:88% position:50% align:center
and their project assignments.

9
00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:42.923 line:88% position:50% align:center
They record expenditure with
proper descriptions and references,

10
00:00:42.933 --> 00:00:46.412 line:88% position:50% align:center
and they review fund requests
and completed projects promptly,

11
00:00:46.422 --> 00:00:49.049 line:88% position:50% align:center
documenting the reasons for their decisions.

12
00:00:50.085 --> 00:00:53.851 line:88% position:50% align:center
And they maintain the system's
settings, review the audit log,

13
00:00:53.861 --> 00:00:56.735 line:88% position:50% align:center
and keep the Board and
project owners informed.

14
00:00:58.385 --> 00:01:01.324 line:88% position:50% align:center
Access is based on the two sign-in roles.

15
00:01:02.385 --> 00:01:05.545 line:88% position:50% align:center
Administrators see every
area of the platform.

16
00:01:06.585 --> 00:01:10.651 line:88% position:50% align:center
Team leaders see only their own
projects, their casual workers,

17
00:01:10.661 --> 00:01:14.511 line:88% position:50% align:center
their logs, their fund requests
and their notifications.

18
00:01:15.552 --> 00:01:18.062 line:88% position:50% align:center
Every person should have their own account.

19
00:01:18.562 --> 00:01:22.862 line:88% position:50% align:center
Accounts should never be shared, because
the audit log identifies people by the

20
00:01:22.872 --> 00:01:24.640 line:88% position:50% align:center
account they signed in with.

21
00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:29.933 line:88% position:50% align:center
When a team leader leaves the organisation,
remove them from their projects,

22
00:01:29.943 --> 00:01:34.061 line:88% position:50% align:center
delete their profile, and ask your technical
administrator to remove their sign-in

23
00:01:34.071 --> 00:01:37.687 line:88% position:50% align:center
account from Firebase, so
that it can no longer be used.

24
00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:43.024 line:88% position:50% align:center
The Settings page begins with
My Profile, showing your name,

25
00:01:43.034 --> 00:01:45.609 line:88% position:50% align:center
username, phone number and role.

26
00:01:46.109 --> 00:01:48.111 line:88% position:50% align:center
We've hidden the phone number here.

27
00:01:49.152 --> 00:01:53.322 line:88% position:50% align:center
Next to it, the Firebase panel
shows the platform's project name,

28
00:01:53.332 --> 00:01:57.241 line:88% position:50% align:center
your unique account identifier, and
whether the connection to the database is

29
00:01:57.251 --> 00:02:01.429 line:88% position:50% align:center
active. Treat your account
identifier as private.

30
00:02:02.485 --> 00:02:06.179 line:88% position:50% align:center
Team leaders see the same
profile and connection panels.

31
00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.908 line:88% position:50% align:center
The SMS configuration is
visible to administrators only.

32
00:02:12.452 --> 00:02:16.641 line:88% position:50% align:center
Let's look, in simple terms,
at how the platform is built.

33
00:02:17.685 --> 00:02:22.005 line:88% position:50% align:center
The application runs in a web
browser, on a computer or a phone.

34
00:02:22.505 --> 00:02:24.415 line:88% position:50% align:center
There's nothing to install.

35
00:02:25.452 --> 00:02:30.351 line:88% position:50% align:center
When someone signs in, their identity
is checked by Firebase Authentication:

36
00:02:30.361 --> 00:02:32.714 line:88% position:50% align:center
Google's secure sign-in service.

37
00:02:33.752 --> 00:02:36.802 line:88% position:50% align:center
The platform's information
is stored in Firestore,

38
00:02:36.812 --> 00:02:39.868 line:88% position:50% align:center
a cloud database also provided by Google.

39
00:02:40.919 --> 00:02:44.399 line:88% position:50% align:center
Firestore holds seven
main collections: users,

40
00:02:44.409 --> 00:02:49.386 line:88% position:50% align:center
projects, casuals, daily
logs, budgets, notifications,

41
00:02:49.396 --> 00:02:50.864 line:88% position:50% align:center
and the audit log.

42
00:02:51.919 --> 00:02:56.505 line:88% position:50% align:center
For SMS, the application sends each
message to a Cloudflare Worker,

43
00:02:56.515 --> 00:03:00.444 line:88% position:50% align:center
which forwards it to Mobilesasa
for delivery to mobile phones.

44
00:03:00.945 --> 00:03:04.372 line:88% position:50% align:center
The application never
contacts Mobilesasa directly;

45
00:03:04.382 --> 00:03:06.358 line:88% position:50% align:center
it always goes through the Worker.

46
00:03:07.985 --> 00:03:10.455 line:88% position:50% align:center
Each collection has a clear purpose.

47
00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:14.494 line:88% position:50% align:center
Users holds administrator
and team leader profiles.

48
00:03:14.992 --> 00:03:18.322 line:88% position:50% align:center
Projects holds project
details and assignments.

49
00:03:18.821 --> 00:03:22.879 line:88% position:50% align:center
And casuals holds worker records,
linked to their projects.

50
00:03:23.919 --> 00:03:26.493 line:88% position:50% align:center
Daily logs holds field reports.

51
00:03:26.994 --> 00:03:31.534 line:88% position:50% align:center
Budgets holds each project's expenditure
and additional fund requests.

52
00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:36.964 line:88% position:50% align:center
Notifications holds in-app alerts, and
audit holds the history of actions.

53
00:03:38.619 --> 00:03:41.350 line:88% position:50% align:center
Security is a shared responsibility.

54
00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:45.896 line:88% position:50% align:center
The platform's protection depends
on several things working together.

55
00:03:46.952 --> 00:03:52.482 line:88% position:50% align:center
Correctly configured Firebase Authentication,
so that only registered users can sign in.

56
00:03:53.519 --> 00:03:58.743 line:88% position:50% align:center
Firestore security rules, which decide
who can read or change each type of record

57
00:03:58.753 --> 00:04:01.510 line:88% position:50% align:center
— not just what the
screens choose to display.

58
00:04:02.552 --> 00:04:05.146 line:88% position:50% align:center
Careful validation of
the information entered,

59
00:04:05.156 --> 00:04:07.418 line:88% position:50% align:center
and good habits from every user.

60
00:04:08.452 --> 00:04:11.547 line:88% position:50% align:center
No system is completely immune to attack.

61
00:04:12.048 --> 00:04:15.586 line:88% position:50% align:center
These controls reduce risk;
they don't eliminate it.

62
00:04:16.084 --> 00:04:19.955 line:88% position:50% align:center
So the technical team should review
the Firestore rules and the Worker's

63
00:04:19.965 --> 00:04:21.862 line:88% position:50% align:center
configuration regularly.

64
00:04:22.885 --> 00:04:28.162 line:88% position:50% align:center
And passwords, configuration values and
keys must never be shared in messages,

65
00:04:28.172 --> 00:04:30.238 line:88% position:50% align:center
screenshots or documents.

66
00:04:31.885 --> 00:04:36.243 line:88% position:50% align:center
Let's bring it together, with best
practices for reliable records.

67
00:04:37.285 --> 00:04:39.782 line:88% position:50% align:center
Enter data accurately the first time.

68
00:04:40.282 --> 00:04:44.797 line:88% position:50% align:center
Check project references, budgets
and phone numbers before saving.

69
00:04:45.819 --> 00:04:48.016 line:88% position:50% align:center
Report daily and honestly.

70
00:04:48.517 --> 00:04:53.116 line:88% position:50% align:center
A short, accurate log submitted on the
day is worth far more than a detailed one

71
00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.141 line:88% position:50% align:center
written from memory a week later.

72
00:04:56.185 --> 00:05:01.129 line:88% position:50% align:center
Describe expenses consistently, and
always include a receipt or reference.

73
00:05:02.152 --> 00:05:06.497 line:88% position:50% align:center
Give clear reasons for every fund
request, and for every decision.

74
00:05:07.552 --> 00:05:12.607 line:88% position:50% align:center
And protect access: keep accounts
personal, sign out on shared devices,

75
00:05:12.617 --> 00:05:15.674 line:88% position:50% align:center
and remove access promptly
when someone leaves.

76
00:05:17.319 --> 00:05:22.010 line:88% position:50% align:center
For Board members and project owners, the
platform offers a dependable basis for

77
00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.336 line:88% position:50% align:center
oversight, provided you
ask the right questions.

78
00:05:26.385 --> 00:05:31.486 line:88% position:50% align:center
Are projects active and reporting regularly,
or have their daily logs gone quiet?

79
00:05:32.519 --> 00:05:36.500 line:88% position:50% align:center
How much of each budget has
been used, and how much remains?

80
00:05:37.552 --> 00:05:41.370 line:88% position:50% align:center
How often are additional funds
requested, for what reasons,

81
00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.746 line:88% position:50% align:center
and how were those requests decided?

82
00:05:44.785 --> 00:05:49.378 line:88% position:50% align:center
And does the audit trail show the expected
people taking the expected actions?

83
00:05:50.419 --> 00:05:53.404 line:88% position:50% align:center
Administrators can walk the
Board through the dashboard,

84
00:05:53.414 --> 00:05:58.254 line:88% position:50% align:center
the financial overview and the audit
log, to answer each of these questions.

85
00:06:00.085 --> 00:06:04.899 line:88% position:50% align:center
This brings the NEWL AFRICA Digital
System Training programme to a close.

86
00:06:05.952 --> 00:06:08.859 line:88% position:50% align:center
You've seen how projects
are created and assigned,

87
00:06:08.869 --> 00:06:12.466 line:88% position:50% align:center
how field activity is reported,
how money is allocated,

88
00:06:12.476 --> 00:06:17.010 line:88% position:50% align:center
requested and approved, and how
notifications and the audit log keep everyone

89
00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.748 line:88% position:50% align:center
informed and accountable.

90
00:06:19.785 --> 00:06:24.729 line:88% position:50% align:center
The platform is a powerful tool, but its
value depends on the people who use it.

91
00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:29.497 line:88% position:50% align:center
Use it responsibly, keep it
accurate, and keep it transparent.

92
00:06:30.552 --> 00:06:32.723 line:88% position:50% align:center
Thank you for completing this training.

93
00:06:35.685 --> 00:06:39.705 line:88% position:50% align:center
This training experience was
produced by KEYPOLE TECHNOLOGIES.
